  "finding": "At sample open each TOP still holds the previous input and must swing to the new one through the bootstrap switch. Discharging toward a mid-scale input (frames 3 and 9, TOPN 0.9 V -> 0.45 V) is the weak direction: body effect on the thick-oxide switch leaves little overdrive at SS -40 C and 0.81 V, so the swing is current-limited (~24 uA, ~19 mV/ns) and then decays with a 4-5 ns tail. The extracted CDAC adds about 0.25 pF per side to the ~1.03 pF sampled capacitance, mostly TOP coupling to the driven bottom plates (~0.2 pF) plus ~52 fF of fixed load, so the same trajectory takes ~25% longer and the tail is ~2 time constants short at close. Scaling all extracted resistance to 1% changes nothing (-0.336 vs -0.351 LSB); removing only the TOP parasitic capacitance restores the schematic result (-0.042 vs -0.038 LSB). The planned fill contributes ~14 fF of the added capacitance.",
  "remedy_options": [
    "Strengthen the bootstrap main switch (more parallel width or bulk bootstrapping) for SS -40 C mid-scale discharge",
    "Lengthen acquisition within the conversion slack (SS -40 C deadline margin is 20.45 ns); this changes the external timing spec",
    "Reduce TOP capacitance; the TOP-to-bottom-plate coupling is intrinsic to the MOM array and routing, so this needs a CDAC redesign"
  ],
